%% FIG-M22-02 — OAuth 2.1 Authorization Code Flow with PKCE Architecture
%% Original, course-owned, editable Mermaid source for Essential CS.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as Resource Owner (User)
    participant Client as Client Application (SPA / Mobile / Web)
    participant Browser as User Agent (Browser)
    participant AS as Authorization Server (IdP / AS)
    participant RS as Resource Server (API)

    Note over Client: 1. Generate high-entropy code_verifier<br/>Compute code_challenge = BASE64URL(SHA256(code_verifier))<br/>Store code_verifier securely in local session state

    Client->>Browser: 2. Redirect to /authorize with:<br/>client_id, redirect_uri, scope, state,<br/>code_challenge, code_challenge_method=S256
    Browser->>AS: 3. Forward authorization request
    AS->>User: 4. Authenticate user & display consent prompt
    User->>AS: 5. User submits credentials & approves scope
    AS->>Browser: 6. 302 Redirect to redirect_uri with:<br/>authorization_code, state
    Browser->>Client: 7. Forward authorization_code & state

    Note over Client: 8. Verify state matches local state<br/>Prepare token exchange request

    Client->>AS: 9. POST /token (backchannel / direct)<br/>grant_type=authorization_code, code,<br/>redirect_uri, client_id, code_verifier

    Note over AS: 10. PKCE Verification:<br/>Compute SHA256(code_verifier)<br/>Assert SHA256(code_verifier) == stored code_challenge<br/>(Binds exchange to possession of verifier from the original authorization transaction;<br/>does NOT authenticate client identity)

    AS->>Client: 11. Return JSON response:<br/>access_token, token_type=Bearer, expires_in, (refresh_token)

    Client->>RS: 12. GET /api/resource<br/>Authorization: Bearer <access_token>
    RS->>Client: 13. Verify token claims & return resource data

    Note over Client,RS: Core Boundary: OAuth is authorization delegation, not authentication by itself!<br/>PKCE mitigates authorization-code interception/misuse when the attacker lacks code_verifier (RFC 9700 / RFC 7636);<br/>it does not protect a fully compromised client device or solve all OAuth threats.
